    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0371" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/12–248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d305-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-04T11:00:00-05:00">December 4, 1948—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2104. Dept opinion not desirable provide American guard (urtel 2611 Dec 2 rptd
                    Nanking 1972) as part international force for UN Hqrs, Shanghai. Appropriate
                    assistance to UN foreign representatives should be provided under US Govt
                    emergency plans to assist evacuation foreign nationals.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d305-f1" n="11" type="source" xml:id="d305-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in China as telegram No. 1771.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
